<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 19 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 19 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,573.1 billion levs on November 22 from 1,321.7</p>
<p>billion levs on November 15, preliminary central bank figures</p>
<p>showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government rose 15.29 percent to 626.6 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 21.81 percent to 431.1</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms rose</p>
<p>3.36 percent to 135.2 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	  NOV22-NOV15 NOV22-NOV1  NOV 1-SEPT27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	+19.02	+26.83	 +1.67</p>
<p> Credit to govt		 +15.29	+23.54	 +2.26</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	+21.81	+29.77	 +2.40</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms +3.36	 +2.89	 -1.94</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	NOV 22	NOV 15	  NOV 1</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,573.1     1,321.7	1,240.3</p>
<p> Credit to govt		   626.6	 543.5	  507.2</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  431.1	 353.9	  332.2</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  135.2	 130.8	  131.4</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms    1.10	  1.11	   1.12</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
